  "caption": "Quinn bought a massage gun with nine speeds, then a foam roller, then another one. The mission: break up every knot and flush out the toxins.\n\nThe reality: these tools can make muscles feel looser and less sore for a while, mostly by calming the nervous system. They don't really break knots, release fascia or flush anything, and they don't speed recovery much.\n\nWhat often helps: use them as comfort tools, add a brief roll to your warm-up, keep strength work in the plan, and avoid bony areas and swollen or broken skin. Sleep, food and sensible training load matter more.\n\nIf one spot needs the gun every single day, pain persists, or you have a circulation or clotting condition, ask first.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
